{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil Times New Roman;}{\f1\fswiss Arial;}{\f2\fswiss Calibri;}}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qc\f1\fs28\b Student Management System Using Java Full Stack Technologies\b0\par\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\f2\fs20\par\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\f2\fs18\b Submitted By\b0\par Name: Kanakam Narendra\par Roll/Register Number: 23102A040983\par Department: Computer Science and Engineering\par College: Mohan Babu University\par Academic Year: 2026\par\par\b Guided By\b0\par Guide/Mentor: Hari\par\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\f2\fs20\par\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\f2\fs20\b 1. Abstract\b0\par The Student Management System is a Java Full Stack web application developed to manage student information efficiently. The system allows authorized users to add, view, update, and delete student records through a user-friendly web interface. The application uses a Java-based backend to process business logic and communicate with the database. The frontend provides an interactive interface for users, while the database stores student details securely. This project demonstrates the practical use of full-stack development concepts, including frontend design, backend development, database management, REST APIs, and application integration.\par\par\b 2. Introduction\b0\par In educational institutions, managing student information manually can be time-consuming and may lead to errors. A computerized student management system helps institutions store and manage student information in an organized and reliable manner. This project provides a centralized system for maintaining student records such as name, roll number, department, email address, phone number, and academic details. The application improves efficiency, reduces paperwork, and provides quick access to information.\par\par\b 3. Objectives\b0\par - To develop a complete Java Full Stack web application.\par - To manage student records digitally.\par - To provide create, read, update, and delete operations.\par - To reduce manual paperwork and data entry errors.\par - To provide a simple and user-friendly interface.\par - To store information securely in a relational database.\par - To implement communication between frontend and backend using REST APIs.\par - To understand real-world software development practices.\par\par\b 4. Technologies Used\b0\par\b Frontend\b0\par - HTML5\par - CSS3\par - JavaScript\par - React.js\par\par\b Backend\b0\par - Java\par - Spring Boot\par - Spring MVC\par - Spring Data JPA\par - REST APIs\par\par\b Database\b0\par - MySQL\par\par\b Development Tools\b0\par - IntelliJ IDEA or Eclipse\par - Visual Studio Code\par - MySQL Workbench\par - Postman\par - Git and GitHub\par - Apache Maven\par\par\b 5. System Modules\b0\par\b 5.1 User Login Module\b0\par This module provides secure access to the application. Authorized users can log in using their username and password.\par\par\b 5.2 Student Registration Module\b0\par This module allows the administrator to add new student details, including name, roll number, department, email, phone number, and year of study.\par\par\b 5.3 Student View Module\b0\par Users can view the complete list of registered students. Student information can be displayed in a structured table.\par\par\b 5.4 Student Update Module\b0\par This module allows users to modify existing student information when required.\par\par\b 5.5 Student Delete Module\b0\par The administrator can remove outdated or incorrect student records from the system.\par\par\b 5.6 Search Module\b0\par Users can search for students using details such as name, roll number, or department.\par\par\b 5.7 Database Module\b0\par This module stores and retrieves student details from the MySQL database using Spring Data JPA.\par\par\b 6. System Architecture\b0\par The application follows a three-layer architecture.\par\par\b Presentation Layer\b0\par The presentation layer contains the user interface developed using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and React.js.\par\par\b Business Logic Layer\b0\par The business logic layer is developed using Java and Spring Boot. It processes user requests and applies application rules.\par\par\b Data Access Layer\b0\par The data access layer communicates with the MySQL database using Spring Data JPA and Hibernate.\par\par\b 7. Project Workflow\b0\par 1. The user opens the application.\par 2. The user logs in to the system.\par 3. The user selects an operation such as add, view, update, delete, or search.\par 4. The frontend sends a request to the backend through a REST API.\par 5. The backend processes the request.\par 6. The database performs the required operation.\par 7. The result is sent back to the frontend.\par 8. The result is displayed to the user.\par\par\b 8. Advantages\b0\par - Easy to use and maintain.\par - Reduces manual work.\par - Provides fast access to student information.\par - Improves data accuracy.\par - Supports centralized data management.\par - Reduces paperwork.\par - Provides organized and secure record storage.\par - Can be expanded with additional features.\par\par\b 9. Future Enhancements\b0\par - Student attendance management.\par - Marks and examination management.\par - Online fee payment.\par - Email and SMS notifications.\par - Admin and student role-based access.\par - Cloud database integration.\par - Mobile application support.\par - Report generation in PDF format.\par - Advanced dashboard and analytics.\par - Deployment on cloud platforms.\par\par\b 10. Conclusion\b0\par The Student Management System Using Java Full Stack Technologies successfully demonstrates the development of a complete web application using frontend, backend, and database technologies. The project provides an efficient way to manage student information and reduces the difficulties associated with manual record maintenance. Through this project, practical knowledge of Java, Spring Boot, React.js, REST APIs, MySQL, and full-stack application development is gained. The project can be further enhanced by adding attendance, examination, payment, notification, and cloud deployment features.\par\par\b 11. Declaration\b0\par I, Kanakam Narendra, bearing Roll/Register Number 23102A040983, hereby declare that the project titled Student Management System Using Java Full Stack Technologies is prepared as part of my academic work under the guidance of Hari, Mohan Babu University.\par\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qc\f2\fs18\par\b Student Signature:\b0 ____________________\par Name: Kanakam Narendra\par Date: 2026\par}\par